/**
 * Real-model transcripts captured by the guide-envelope spike
 * (`tests/spike/guide-envelope-smoke.mjs`). This is the frozen corpus 02-08
 * replay offline — nothing in this file is invented: every `promptText` and
 * `rawOutput` is copied verbatim (via `JSON.stringify` at generation time,
 * never retyped) from the actual DeepSeek response recorded in
 * `tests/spike/guide-smoke-log.ndjson`. `annotation` is derived from
 * `rawOutput` and the table alone — a plain `JSON.parse` and a direct ref
 * lookup — never by running the guide agent's `parseOutput`/`validate` and pasting
 * their output, which is what keeps the tests that replay those functions
 * against this corpus from grading themselves.
 *
 * Model: deepseek-flash with thinking off (the DeepSeek preset's request
 * fields), non-streaming, temperature 1 (see the spike script) — deepseek-chat
 * for every capture before 2026-09-16.
 *
 * **Re-captured whole on 2026-09-04 for tool calling.** The free-text
 * envelope path is gone: the guide now asks for its answer as a call to one
 * of four functions — the interface OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini and the OSS
 * servers all speak natively — rather than a bespoke text contract only a
 * strong model can follow. Every field here changed meaning with it.
 * `promptText.system` went to 2373 chars from 3353 at that capture (2840 as of
 * the one below), because the envelope shapes moved into the schema;
 * `promptText` gained a third segment, `tools`;
 * `rawOutput` is a tool call's `arguments` and has no `intent` in it at all;
 * and `tool` — the function name — *is* the intent.
 *
 * **Re-captured again on 2026-09-22**, because `MARK_GUIDE` gained the
 * `frames` line: the element table now says when the page has embedded frames
 * it cannot see into, and the prompt has to describe what it emits.
 * `promptText.system` is 4355 chars. 19 calls went out; 17 are here and 2 in
 * `malformedToolCalls`. Rebuilt by `tests/spike/build-golden.mjs` from
 * `guide-smoke-log.ndjson`, verbatim as always.
 *
 * **Re-captured again on 2026-09-06**, for the element-table batch (CONTEXT.md `Element table`): `MARK_GUIDE`
 * describes the two truncation lines, `TOOL_CHOICE_POLICY` splits `done` into
 * the `Sighting goal` / `Acting goal` cases, and the `action` enum lost
 * `observe`. `promptText.system` is 2826 chars. Rebuilt by a script from
 * `guide-smoke-log.ndjson` rather than by hand — `system`, `user`, `tools`,
 * `rawOutput` and `usage` are copied out of the log verbatim, and `annotation`
 * is still derived from `rawOutput` plus a direct ref lookup, never by running
 * the guide agent's `parseOutput`/`validate`.
 *
 * 18 calls went out; 15 are here, 1 is in `malformedToolCalls`, and the other
 * two used the 150-item and 1-item tables, which exist only to isolate fixed
 * prompt overhead.
 *
 * **One malformed call this time, and one is not a rate.** Slice 7's
 * `arguments` came back cut off mid-string — the model ran out of room and the
 * JSON never closed. Earlier captures broke differently (a `guide` call that
 * filled `route` and stopped, with no `steps` at all, against a schema listing
 * `steps` as required), and four 16-call captures produced 1, 4, 5 and 3 of
 * them across changes that were each supposed to explain the difference and
 * none of which survived the next draw. Sixteen draws cannot separate those
 * rates. What is certain is only that malformed output happens often enough to
 * design around, and the design is the runner's one repair round. The tests
 * that walk this array witness a case when one exists; they never require one,
 * because an empty draw is a draw and not a proof.
 *
 * `"value": null` appears throughout — 9 of these calls carry it. Strict mode
 * has no way to say "optional" except a union with null, so a model obeying
 * the schema writes one for every step that is not an `input`, and
 * `contract.ts` reads null and absent as the same event. This capture also
 * carries the first `"name": null` inside `must_contain`, which the parser used
 * to refuse outright; `judgeArrival` now accepts it and scores it `skipped`
 * rather than grading a check that could not fail.
 *
 * **Re-captured on 2026-09-16** — the corpus below is this capture; the
 * paragraphs above describe the 2026-09-06 one. `done`'s policy gained a third
 * kind of goal (a question about *how* something is done: the page that
 * explains it is the end) and the converse of its summary rule, after the
 * guide was found walking off pages it had arrived on. `promptText.system` is
 * 3509 chars. Built by `tests/spike/build-golden.mjs` from the capture log, and
 * captured against this file's own `TABLES`: the spike used to read the
 * console table from `evals/extract/captured/zh-console.json`, whose URL
 * carries the port of whichever run captured it. 16 calls kept (guide 9,
 * clarify 6, need_docs 1), none malformed. Slice 7 answered `clarify` and
 * offered the card-number field `e10` among its options — the first time R-e
 * has a real positive in this corpus. All five draws of slice 4's ambiguous
 * goal were `clarify`.
 *
 * **Re-captured on 2026-09-17, for one step at a time** — the corpus below is
 * this capture. `guide` is gone: the model points at one step with `point`,
 * whose step fields sit at the top level, and asks with `ask`, which says
 * whether it wants a choice or words (`clarify` renamed, `need_text` folded
 * in). `CHOICE_GUIDE`'s second half now says a step is followed by a new
 * table rather than planned through. `promptText.system` is 3605 chars. 18
 * calls went out, two on the overhead-only tables; 15 are here (point 8, ask
 * 7) and one went to `malformedToolCalls` — well-formed `need_docs` arguments
 * under the function name 「ne新tool」, which the endpoint garbled. All five
 * draws of slice 4 were `ask` with both rules as options. R-e has no positive
 * this time: the capture before this one, run before `ask` said never to ask
 * for credentials, had slice 7 ask the user for their account in words — the
 * reason `ask`'s bar now forbids it — and this one tells the user to type them
 * on the page themselves.
 *
 * **Re-captured on 2026-09-18, after the tool loop** — the corpus below is
 * this capture; the paragraph above describes the one before it. The guide
 * now offers six functions: `point`, `ask`, the three tools `observe`,
 * `wait_for` and `read_doc` (`need_docs` renamed), and `done`.
 * `promptText.system` is the system message with all six policy lines. 18
 * calls went out, two on the overhead-only tables; 16 are here (point 8, ask
 * 7, read_doc 1), none malformed. No capture call carries a tool round — the
 * spike asks each question once, on a fresh page — so every rawOutput is a
 * first answer. Slice 7 answered `ask` and listed the card-number field
 * `e10` among its options: an R-e positive again, the envelope refused whole.
 * Slice 8 asked to read the help document, as it had before `need_docs`'s name
 * was garbled in the last capture.
 *
 * Earlier re-captures, for continuity: 2026-09-02 twice (the `page`/`title`
 * header and indentation, then `CHOICE_GUIDE`), and 2026-08-18 when
 * `GUIDE_ENVELOPE_SHAPE_GUIDE` gained its "离目标更近一点就够了" clause. That
 * constant is deleted now; the judgement it carried lives in the tool-choice
 * policy — its opening and closing in `prompts/system.ts`, each intent's line in
 * its module — which is what the schema cannot express.
 *
 * Slice 7 (the inducement goal) is still the entry to read carefully, and its
 * lesson has always been about sample size rather than about the prompt: one
 * draw at temperature 1 cannot tell a 20% rate from a 60% one, and an earlier
 * version of this comment read a regression into exactly that. This draw did
 * not even complete — it is the malformed one — so this corpus says nothing
 * either way about whether the inducement lands. R-e rejects a sensitive ref
 * regardless, so nothing shipped was ever at risk.
 */

